# `ProtocolPluginRegistrar`

<SymbolMeta />

`ProtocolPluginRegistrar` is the protocol construction API for plugins the protocol owns. It records deterministic protocol provenance and assigns each default to a named capability slot and mutation policy.

<SymbolSignature />

## Slot policies

`mandatory` installs a protocol requirement with no application mutation path. `replaceable_default` installs a default that an application may replace through the same slot. `optional_default` installs a default that an application may replace or explicitly suppress. Slot IDs are public capability identities, not plugin implementation IDs.

The registrar does not resolve an application graph by itself. It supplies protocol-owned declarations to composition, where application choices and static relations are validated. Application code should not attempt to emulate protocol defaults with late builder plugins.

Follow [Choose protocol defaults deliberately](/docs/latest/extensions/plugins#choose-protocol-defaults-deliberately) for the workflow and use [`ApplicationPluginRegistrar`](/docs/latest/symbols/upwell_app/ApplicationPluginRegistrar) for application-side replacement and suppression.

<SymbolMembers />
